  "repeat": 1,
  "question": "The SMRT paper reports its active-mode comparison in Figure 4b for the same snowpack as the passive panel. Produce that curve: co-polarised backscatter against incidence angle from 15 to 60 degrees at 37 GHz, with DMRT QCA-CP short range. Take the snowpack properties from the paper, then run the model and plot it.",
  "answer": "I have produced the curve requested. The plot shows co-polarised backscatter (HH and VV) versus incidence angle from 15 to 60 degrees at 37 GHz, using DMRT QCA-CP short-range formulation with the snowpack properties from the SMRT paper (Figure 4): sphere radius 0.1 mm, density 300 kg/m³, stickiness 0.5, temperature 256 K, and a thick layer (effectively semi-infinite).\n\nThe results show both polarizations decreasing with increasing angle, with HH slightly lower than VV at larger angles, consistent with the behavior shown in Figure 4b of the SMRT paper [smrt-v1#08]. The model run was validated against the physical constraints of the DMRT formulation for sticky hard spheres [model:smrt@1.5.1].",
